{"id": "g2_distinct_mod4_three_positive", "signature": "solve(samples)", "statement": "Given a list of integers `samples`, count how many DISTINCT values v in it satisfy v > 0 and v % 4 == 3 (Python's % operator, so the remainder is always in 0..3). Repeated values are counted once. Zero and negative values are never counted. Return 0 if there are none, including for an empty list.", "tests": [{"args": [[]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[3]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[3, 3, 3]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[-1]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[7, 11, 15, 3]], "expected": 4}, {"args": [[1, 2, 4, 8, 0]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[-5, -9, 3, 7, 3]], "expected": 2}, {"args": [[19, 19, 23, 27, 27, 31]], "expected": 4}, {"args": [[1000003, 1000003, 0]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[-3, -7, -11]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[2, 6, 10, 14]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[43, 47, 51, 55, 59]], "expected": 5}, {"args": [[0]], "expected": 0}], "facts": [["arg", "samples", "int_list"], ["iterate", "samples"], ["keep", "positive"], ["remainder", "4", "3"], ["aggregate", "distinct_count"], ["size", "samples", "tiny"]], "deps": {"schema": ["seq_fold"], "uses": [], "solution_sha256": "db38095fb82620a67d336ccba5f6a284c414431051857d85937bab82db7bbb8f", "reference_sha256": "f5e49d5e0f120aa41c0919767e18f45f47074086bebc6be54a8e3190e47b6fb4"}}